  "instance_name": "infantilization_stereotype",
  "label": "Infantilization Stereotype",
  "description": "The meme uses the image of a child standing between two large costumed characters to imply that the child is 'classic' or 'authentic' in a way that is not appropriate or respectful. This relies on the real-world stereotype that children are inherently 'classic' or 'authentic' versions of things, which can be seen as infantilizing or objectifying the child. This stereotype is part of broader ableist and ageist tropes that reduce individuals to their perceived developmental stage.",
